1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,000
How do habits take shape? Repeated actions can grow more automatic over time.

2
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:07,950
There is no universal twenty-one-day rule. Habit formation varies widely.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,900
Stress or fatigue can make starting difficult. Try a smaller first step.

4
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:15,850
An enjoyable linchpin habit can make other helpful actions easier.

5
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:19,800
Rehearse the first few concrete steps before you begin.

6
00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:23,750
A habit includes what comes before, the action itself, and what follows.

7
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:27,700
Work with your daily energy levels instead of relying on a rigid clock.

8
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:31,650
Treat twenty-one days as an experiment, not a deadline. Missing a day is normal.

9
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:35,600
After catching an unhelpful pattern, add a small positive replacement.

10
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:39,550
Real progress looks like less effort and more flexibility across situations.
